  "title": "Animals",
  "description": "Learn the names of common animals and how to describe what they do.",
  "guidebook": "Welcome to the animal kingdom! In Spanish, all animals have a grammatical gender, just like other nouns. For example, *el perro* (the dog) is masculine, while *la vaca* (the cow) is feminine. When describing what animals do, we use simple verbs. To say 'the cat drinks milk', we say *El gato bebe leche*. Notice how the verb changes depending on who is doing the action: *bebe* (drinks) or *come* (eats). Remember, fish that are swimming in the water are called *el pez*, but if they are on a plate, they are *el pescado*. Let's stick to the living ones for now! Have fun meeting your new animal friends!",
